.TH sane\-plustek8200i 5 "07 Oct 2026" "@PACKAGEVERSION@" "SANE Scanner Access Now Easy"
.IX sane\-plustek8200i
.SH NAME
sane\-plustek8200i \- SANE backend for the Plustek OpticFilm 8200i (GL128)
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B sane\-plustek8200i
library implements a SANE (Scanner Access Now Easy) backend that provides
access to the Genesys GL128 based Plustek OpticFilm 8200i film scanner:
.PP
.RS
.ft CR
.nf
Vendor  Product  Chipset  Connection
------  -------  -------  ----------
0x07b3  0x1825   GL128    USB
.fi
.ft R
.RE
.PP
.B Note:
an older scanner sells under the same model name but reports USB product ID
.BR 0x130d ,
and uses a GL845. That one is driven by
.BR sane\-genesys (5),
not by this backend. Identify the device by its USB ID or chipset rather
than by its model name.
.PP
This is a transparency-only scanner: there is no flatbed mode. The device
has a fourth, infrared illuminant that this backend uses to detect and
repair dust and scratches.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-mode Color|Gray|Infrared|Color+Infrared
Selects the scan mode.
.B Color
delivers RGB and
.B Gray
a single averaged channel.
.B Infrared
delivers only the infrared channel, in which film dye is transparent, so
that physical defects alone remain.
.B Color+Infrared
delivers two SANE frames: the colour image, then its pixel-aligned
infrared plane as a gray frame. SANE has no standard four-channel frame
format, so a frontend must accept multiple frames to use it;
.BR scanimage (1)
cannot save the second frame.
.TP
.B \-\-resolution 300|600|1200|2400|3600|7200
Scan resolution in dpi. Above roughly 1490 dpi the vertical sampling is
set by the line rate against the motor speed, so the higher settings are
upsampled vertically to the resolution they report.
.TP
.B \-\-depth 8|16
Bits per channel. The sensor is 16 bit; 8 bit keeps the high byte of each
sample.
.TP
.B \-\-ir\-clean[=yes|no]
Make an additional infrared pass and repair dust and scratches in the
colour image from it. This roughly doubles the scan time.
.TP
.B \-\-auto\-wb[=yes|no]
Scale the colour channels so that their means match. Off by default,
because negative conversion and colour profiling need the sensor's
calibrated response unchanged.
.TP
.B \-\-exposure 1.0..4.0
Light integration time as a multiple of the default. The carriage slows
down to preserve the geometry, so the scan takes proportionally longer.
For dense negatives and dark slides.
.TP
.B \-l \-t \-x \-y
The scan window, in millimetres, within the film frame.
.SH IMAGE DATA
As required by the SANE standard, 16 bit samples are delivered in the
.B native byte order of the host
the backend runs on. Frontends that write a fixed-endian file format must
byte-swap accordingly, and
.BR saned (8)
reconciles the byte order itself when the client and server differ.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I @CONFIGDIR@/plustek8200i.conf
The backend configuration file.
.TP
.I @LIBDIR@/libsane\-plustek8200i.a
The static library implementing this backend.
.TP
.I @LIBDIR@/libsane\-plustek8200i.so
The shared library implementing this backend (present on systems that
support dynamic loading).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SANE_DEBUG_PLUSTEK8200I
If the library was compiled with debug support enabled, this variable
controls the debug level: 0 errors, 1 adds warnings, 2 adds progress,
3 and above add protocol detail.
.PP
The following are diagnostic aids. They are not a configuration
interface, they are not stable between releases, and a normal scan needs
none of them.
.TP
.B PLUSTEK8200I_REGTRACE=\fIpath\fP
Append every register write, and the phase markers between them, to
.IR path .
Reconstructs the register state at any point of a scan without needing
usbmon (which needs root).
.TP
.B PLUSTEK8200I_DRYRUN=1
Program every image-pass register, then stop before the carriage moves.
With
.B PLUSTEK8200I_REGTRACE
this makes a deterministic fingerprint of everything a scan decides,
which is how changes to the scan path are checked for equivalence.
.TP
.B PLUSTEK8200I_STREAM=0
Read the whole frame before returning from
.BR sane_start ,
instead of streaming it line by line from
.BR sane_read .
Streaming is used by default where it can be.
.TP
.B PLUSTEK8200I_STREAMCHECK=1
Rebuild the frame through the streaming pipeline as well and compare the
two, to verify they agree.
.TP
.B PLUSTEK8200I_SHADING=0
Skip shading calibration and the infrared reference measurement.
.TP
.B PLUSTEK8200I_RAWIMG=\fIpath\fP
Write the raw sensor data, before any processing, to
.IR path .
.TP
.B PLUSTEK8200I_CCD_PROFILE=legacy
Use the older macOS-derived CCD register values instead of the verified
ones. Retained for A/B comparison; it does not produce a usable image.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR sane (7),
.BR sane\-genesys (5),
.BR sane\-usb (5),
.BR scanimage (1),
.BR saned (8)
